    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>A Viking Brujah Embraced around 621 A.D., Bjorn Garinson fled Scandinavia's fall to the Ventrue and Toreador and spent centuries in torpor before waking in colonial America. He leads Washington's leaderless Brujah by default from his Adams-Morgan club, Purgatory, dreaming of a unified Brujah clan someday overthrowing the Camarilla, though his own clan's fractiousness leaves him despairing of ever seeing it happen. He suspects, correctly, that Marcus Vitel may not be a true Ventrue at all.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>It would be easy to play Bjorn as a stereotypical loud, boisterous Viking, but there is more to him: he has suffered the wrath of his own Kindred and is unwilling to endure it again. Party to avoid dealing with reality, but don't take crap from anyone except the Prince.</p>",
    "notes": "Sire: Dark Raven. Disciplines (as printed): Animalism 2, Auspex 4, Celerity 4, Fortitude 3, Obfuscate 1, Potence 5, Presence 3, Protean 2. Haven: Purgatory. Secrets: B. Convert Disciplines by adding owned power Items from the disciplines compendium at Storyteller discretion.",
